{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"bash -lc \\\"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: ANSWER.md\n@@\n+Changes made to fix caching of long‑term memory writes.\n+\n+**What was changed**\n+* \"'`build_system` now returns two separate system‑prompt blocks instead of a single\n+  concatenated string.\n+  * **Static block** – contains the immutable `INSTRUCTIONS`. No `cache_control`\n+    marker is applied, allowing the provider to keep this block hot across all\n+    requests.\n+  * **Volatile block** – contains the per‑athlete context (date, zones, facts,\n+    language). This block is marked `{\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` so only it is\n+    regenerated when `save_fact` updates `a.facts`.\n+* Fixed the malformed `volatile_block` definition that had stray `+` characters.\n+\n+**Why it works**\n+The note described how a single cached prompt caused the whole prompt to be\n+re‑cached after each `save_fact` because any byte change after the cache marker\n+invalidated the suffix. Splitting the prompt into two blocks and marking only the\n+volatile part as `ephemeral` isolates cache invalidation to the tail, preserving\n+the static instructions block and avoiding the full‑prompt cost.\n+\n+**Parts of the note applied**\n+* Split system prompt into two text blocks.\n+* Mark volatile tail with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`.\n+* Keep static instructions without a marker.\n+\n+No other behaviour was altered.\n+\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
